Architectural Roles
Core Domain Model Architectural Roles

##
NOTE:
Godot Rule
Nothing should directly know about everything else.
A Part should not know what the Market is, an Employee should not know what a Company is, and an Order should not know how a machine works. 
Communication should flow through focused services and events, preventing god objects and keeping the project aligned with the Sacred Framework
##

Foundation Layer (Pure Data Definitions)

MaterialDefinition - Static definition of a material type and its starting attributes.

OperationDefinition - Static definition of an operation and the attribute modifications it applies.

EquipmentDefinition - Static definition of a machine type, supported operations, cost, and cycle times.

PartDefinition - Static recipe describing a known material and operation sequence.

NeedDefinition - Static market need template used for generating dynamic needs.

AttributeDefinition-Creates a master list of valid attributes in the game

Industry Definition- Provides the industries used by market generation.

Runtime Domain Layer (Live Game Objects)

Part - Runtime product instance containing a material reference and operation history.

Assembly - Runtime collection of parts and/or subassemblies.

Equipment - Runtime machine placed in the world and capable of performing operations.

Employee - Runtime worker capable of executing work instructions.

Order - Runtime production request specifying the product, quantity, due date, and payment terms required to fulfill a contract.

Need - Runtime market opportunity generated from the market system.

Production Layer

OperationExecution - Represents a single operation currently being performed on a part.

WorkInstruction - Defines work to be performed on a specific part type.

Task - Individual executable employee action such as move, operate, wait, or ship.

ProductionJob - Tracks a product's progress through manufacturing.

Logistics Layer

InventoryContainer - Generic storage object capable of holding assemblies.

ShippingRequest - Incoming or outgoing shipment scheduled by the shipping system.

Delivery - Physical shipment currently traveling through the world.

Location - Logical destination used by logistics and pathfinding systems.

Company Layer

Company - Owns all business assets, employees, equipment, and finances.

Facility - Represents a physical business property such as a garage or warehouse.

Account - Maintains company cash, revenue, expenses, and profit.

AssetRegister - Tracks owned machines, materials, and facilities.

Market Layer

Market - Generates and manages active needs.

SampleSubmission - Evaluation record for a proposed product sample.

Contract - Accepted commercial agreement that creates one or more orders.

IndustryProfile - Defines attribute weighting used during need generation.

World Layer

Player - Represents the business owner and controllable character.

Interactable - Base interface for anything the player can physically use.

Computer - World object used for administrative actions.

ShippingArea - Physical dispatch location where completed orders are staged, loaded, and shipped to customers.

ArrivalArea - Physical receiving location where incoming materials, equipment, and deliveries first enter the facility.

StorageArea - World object used for storing inventory.

ShopFloor - Physical production area that contains equipment, storage, employees, materials, parts, and assemblies

Time Layer

MasterClock - The single authoritative time source for the entire simulation.

ScheduledEvent - Event that occurs at a specific game time.

TimerTask - Runtime countdown tied to the Master Clock.

Calendar - Converts raw time into days, weeks, months, and years.

Service Layer (Managers, Not Data)

PartService - Creates, validates, and modifies parts.

AssemblyService - Creates and manages assemblies.

ProductionService - Coordinates manufacturing activities.

EmployeeService - Assigns and manages employee work.

MarketService - Generates needs and evaluates samples.

ShippingService - Manages deliveries and shipments.

FinanceService - Processes payments, expenses, and profit calculations.
